{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789553542,"nonce":"Sv7gA5JXVb9Hl4f5sBaV+IugB/4=","title":"LLVM tier cannot promote Python loops with aggregate parameters","message":"With an LLVM-enabled zypy, nbody_modified's advance takes two %List headers in its HIR signature. Cranelift passes those aggregates by address; LLVM lowers them by value. The per-function LLVM compiler refuses to install an entry with that incompatible ABI, so the 20,000-step inner loop stays in Cranelift. ZYNTAX_OSR_TRACE=1 reports \"LLVM promotion unavailable for advance: aggregate ABI\". This also affects zb_list_extend_any and zb_dict_find.\n\nA safe fix needs a shared cross-tier aggregate ABI or an entry adapter that preserves mutations to list headers. Spilling a by-value copy is invalid: zb_list_extend_any updates its list header during realloc. After the ABI is fixed, verify an LLVM OSR transfer during nbody_modified and compare the checked 50-trial score with PyPy.","files":null}]}